a unary operator applies to the whole unary expression that follows.

ONE CALL, AND IT WAS THE ONLY UNARY OPERATOR THAT NEVER GOT THE RULE. The
unary-minus branch called primary_expr; the `!` branch twenty lines below it
calls postfix_expr, and the cast branch carries the same correction in the same
words. So `-p->v` consumed only `p` and left `->v` to the caller:

    g.v  = -g.v;      fine      -- a member of a plain variable
    p->v = -(p->v);   fine      -- the parentheses group it by hand
    t    = -p->v;     SIGSEGV

WHERE IT BIT, AND IT IS NOT A CORNER. tcc's assembler negates an immediate with
one line, through a pointer:

    if (op == '-') pe->v = -pe->v;                      tccasm.c:178

so mc-tcc segfaulted on EVERY NEGATIVE IMMEDIATE IN ASSEMBLY, while every
positive one assembled:

    stp x29,x30,[sp,-16]!   crash        stp x29,x30,[sp,16]!   fine
    ldr x0,[sp,-8]          crash        ldr x0,[sp,8]          fine
    mov x0,-16              crash        mov x0,16              fine

HOW IT SURFACED. stage0-stage4-complete puts the seed's mc-tcc where the
reference arm puts a host-built tcc, and its first run reached RUNG 2 of the
stage-4 ladder: 1340 of musl's 1349 sources compiled, a 3.2 MB libc.a from 1273
objects, and no crt1.o. Nine files would not compile and every one of them
reported

    SIGNAL 11 -- no diagnostic

so there was nothing to read and the shape had to be found instead. Seven of
the nine are assembly or pull in a file-scope asm block: crt/aarch64/crti.s,
src/string/aarch64/memcpy.S, src/string/aarch64/memset.S among them. No crt1.o
means nothing can be LINKED, so rung 2 stops the entire climb.

THE CONTROL IS WHAT MADE IT ATTRIBUTABLE. A gcc-hosted tcc, built from the same
tarball with the same tcc-arm64-asm series and configured --cpu=arm64,
assembles all of those. The assembler is right; the compiler that built it was
not. With this patch mc-tcc assembles musl's crti.s to an object BYTE-IDENTICAL
to that control's, and the same holds for each instruction above.

MEASURED, LOCALLY, EITHER SIDE:

    difftest amd64        99 -> 99 pass, 0 fail   (case 120 new, and passes)
    difftest aarch64     101 -> 101 pass, 0 fail
    stage 2 corpus       419 of 426               unchanged
    tests2 through mc-tcc 90 of 105               unchanged
    self-compilation      gen2.o == gen3.o        unchanged
    archive round trip    links and runs -> 5     unchanged
    dynamic output        2875-byte shared object unchanged

    musl crti.s           byte-identical to the gcc-built control, 1035 bytes

